 "description": "Revoke one client's authorization from a deployment's Tor v3 service. Use its name from impreza_onion_auth_list. The app, onion identity and other clients remain; the name can later be authorized with a fresh keypair. Removing the last authorized client makes the onion service public: explain that consequence before confirmation. Requires manage scope, customer confirmation and an agent supporting onion-auth-v1. If confirm_token is absent from this connection's input schema, use a connection that exposes it or a supported customer-portal flow. A quote or confirmation request is not completion. IRREVERSIBLE \u2014 takes two calls: the first returns a confirm_token and changes nothing, the second repeats the same arguments plus confirm_token and executes.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "deployment_id": {
    "description": "The dpl_\u2026 deployment id (from impreza_list_deployments).",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "name": {
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "deployment_id",
   "name"
  ],
  "type": "object"
 },
 "name": "impreza_onion_auth_revoke",
